 "version": 1,
 "source_rig": "SK_UEFN_Mannequin (GASP, UE 5.8)",
 "target_rig": "player_woman_skeleton",
 "notes": [
  "Each entry maps one CP body bone (game index 0..72) to one GASP bone.",
  "mode=aim: target world rotation = B_src(t) * B_cp_rest^T * Q_cp_rest, where B = orthonormal basis (d, s, d x s); d = direction from the bone head to the 'aim' bone head (CP aim bone, GASP = its mapped bone), s = secondary axis (see 'secondary').",
  "mode=world: target world rotation = dQ_src(t) * Q_cp_rest (dQ = source world delta from its bind pose); used where both rest poses are anatomically the same in world (upright head, flat toes).",
  "mode=inherit: like world, but premultiplied by the parent's reference alignment R_ref(parent) (finger tips).",
  "secondary.type: carry_axis = world axis in the bind pose of both rigs carried by the source bone (or 'src_bone' if given); live_pair = vector between two bone heads evaluated per frame (CP rest / source live); carry_pair = rest vector between two bone heads carried by the source bone.",
  "Spine choice by normalized height between hips and neck (CP Hips->Neck vs GASP pelvis->neck_01): CP Spine 0.169 / Spine1 0.289 / Spine2 0.446 / Spine3 0.647; GASP spine_01 0.137 / spine_02 0.284 / spine_03 0.406 / spine_04 0.569 / spine_05 0.771. Nearest heads: Spine<-spine_01, Spine1<-spine_02, Spine2<-spine_03, Spine3<-spine_04. Spine3 aims at Neck (=neck_01), so the bend of spine_05 is kept in the Spine3 direction; its roll/twist is carried by spine_05 (the chest bone that parents clavicles and neck in GASP).",
  "Thumb: CP has InHandThumb + Thumb1 + Thumb2, GASP thumb_01..03 (no thumb metacarpal): thumb_01->InHandThumb, thumb_02->Thumb1, thumb_03->Thumb2."
 ],
